# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/

# --- Weights & Biases -------------------------------------------------------
# Live W&B run payloads are large and machine-written. Provenance lives in
# runs/<experiment_id>/resolved_config.json (which records wandb_run_id), so
# nothing scientific is lost by not tracking these.
wandb/
code/wandb/

# --- Per-run output directories (plan.md 2.2) -------------------------------
# runs/<experiment_id>/ IS the canonical record, so the small provenance and
# metric files ARE tracked (updated_rules.md 9: every figure must be traceable
# to exact run IDs). Only the large or regenerable payloads are excluded.
#
# T-LA.1: these two rules are DELIBERATELY OVERRIDDEN with `git add -f` for the
# canonical language cells, and the override is the reason the MoRE arm still
# exists. The five MoRE checkpoints were trained on a rented V100 and committed;
# the MoE and MoR checkpoints were not, the instance was released, and ~25
# GPU-hours had to be re-run to recover weights that every checkpoint evaluation
# (held-out test split, difficulty-stratified loss, OOD perplexity) depends on.
# A `canonical_lang_b` checkpoint is therefore treated as EVIDENCE, not weight:
# it is not regenerable in practice, because reproducing it costs hours on a
# thermally-throttled laptop and lands at a slightly different point in seed
# noise. The rule below still applies to everything else, which is the point --
# exploratory and smoke checkpoints stay out.
#
# Force-add only cells that carry BOTH checkpoint.pt and metrics.json:
#   for d in runs/langB_*/; do [ -f "$d/checkpoint.pt" ] && \
#     [ -f "$d/metrics.json" ] && git add -f "$d/checkpoint.pt"; done
# A checkpoint WITHOUT metrics is an interrupted run at an unknown epoch, and is
# exactly the artifact that reaches a results table by accident -- never commit
# one. A bare `git add -f runs/**/checkpoint.pt` does commit one; the guard above
# refuses it by construction.
runs/**/checkpoint.pt
runs/**/*.pt
runs/**/stdout.log

# T-LA.1: matrix-level console logs from the _launch_*.ps1 helpers. These tee a
# whole multi-run job, so they are not attached to any single run and by
# CLAUDE.md 5 can never be provenance -- the per-run record is
# runs/<experiment_id>/stdout.log, which is itself untracked above. Ignored
# rather than forbidden because teeing a 15 h job is the right thing to do; what
# is not right is committing the tee.
runs/_*.log

# T-LX.8: stray logs at the REPO ROOT, from `python ... > foo.log` invocations.
# CLAUDE.md 5 is per-run output directories only; a root-level log is by
# construction not attached to a run, so it can never be provenance and must
# never be mistaken for it. Ignored rather than forbidden because redirecting a
# long job's output is legitimate -- what is not legitimate is committing it.
# Anything worth keeping belongs in runs/<experiment_id>/stdout.log.
/*.log

# --- Invalidated history: NOT tracked ---------------------------------------
# `archive/` holds every artifact the project has declared INVALIDATED: the
# pre-finalization sweep, undeclared-group runs, crashed runs, 1-epoch smoke
# runs and the superseded dataset snapshots. AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md say so
# explicitly, and the exporter refuses them on provenance grounds, so nothing
# citable lives here.
#
# It is untracked for three reasons, in order of weight:
#
#   1. IDENTITY. The raw W&B run payloads under
#      archive/pre_finalization/wandb_runs_*/ carry two author email
#      addresses, two W&B entity names that embed an institution, a machine
#      hostname and the GitHub account that owns this repository -- 168 tracked
#      files in all. An anonymized review copy must contain none of it, and
#      scrubbing that many machine-written payloads is far more error-prone
#      than not shipping them. Dropping the tree removes the largest identity
#      surface in the repository in a single move.
#   2. SIZE. ~232 MB, of which ~215 MB is checkpoints and the two superseded
#      dataset snapshots. None of it is needed to reproduce any result.
#   3. SIGNAL. 4,016 files of voided history beside the live tree is noise, and
#      a reviewer asking "how do I reproduce this" should not have to navigate
#      it.
#
# This is NOT a deletion. The directory and every file in it remain on disk
# (CLAUDE.md 6, "archive, never delete, evidence"), and the retained tree is
# still the authoritative record of what was invalidated and why -- see the
# INVALIDATED.md notices it carries and the `code/mark_invalidated.py` tool
# that stamps them. Only TRACKING is declined, exactly as for invalidated
# checkpoints below.
#
# The stamping tool used to live at archive/mark_invalidated.py and is now at
# code/mark_invalidated.py, because a tool a fresh clone needs must not live
# inside an untracked tree. It still targets archive/ by default and still
# refuses to run when that directory is absent.
archive/

# --- Model checkpoints outside runs/ ----------------------------------------
# Checkpoints are excluded everywhere except the canonical language matrix,
# which force-adds them (see the runs/ rules above) because they are the
# evidence every checkpoint-based evaluation depends on.
#
# T11.5: the exception that once allowed `!archive/pre_finalization/**/*.pt`
# is GONE. Those checkpoints were tracked as evidence of the pre-audit state,
# but they are not tracked now, for the identity reason above -- that payload
# carries author email addresses, W&B entity names and a machine hostname. The
# evidence a reader needs from that tree is that it was invalidated and why,
# which lives in the INVALIDATED.md notices, not in the weights. The files
# remain on disk.
*.pt
#
# The 15 ADMITTED canonical language checkpoints are the exception, and they
# are listed ONE BY ONE rather than by glob. A glob (`!runs/langB_*/`) was
# tried first and it was wrong: it matched every exploratory and interrupted
# langB_* run, not just the admitted cells, and pulled 49 extra checkpoints
# totalling 1,045 MB of weights into the repository -- none of them citable,
# several of them from runs that never finished. The admitted set is exactly
# the 15 cells in results/language/results.json, and naming them explicitly
# makes a new run's checkpoint stay ignored until someone decides it is
# canonical.
!runs/langB_MoE_seed42__51000018/checkpoint.pt
!runs/langB_MoE_seed43__7d85fe81/checkpoint.pt
!runs/langB_MoE_seed44__c348b39a/checkpoint.pt
!runs/langB_MoE_seed45__64800f08/checkpoint.pt
!runs/langB_MoE_seed46__3d9d12a9/checkpoint.pt
!runs/langB_MoRE_seed42__9cfd3f1c/checkpoint.pt
!runs/langB_MoRE_seed43__dbe38cbd/checkpoint.pt
!runs/langB_MoRE_seed44__16027752/checkpoint.pt
!runs/langB_MoRE_seed45__f6c47448/checkpoint.pt
!runs/langB_MoRE_seed46__d069325c/checkpoint.pt
!runs/langB_MoR_seed42__c93f0fe8__r2/checkpoint.pt
!runs/langB_MoR_seed43__8b54a65f/checkpoint.pt
!runs/langB_MoR_seed44__c11db02d/checkpoint.pt
!runs/langB_MoR_seed45__4041a890/checkpoint.pt
!runs/langB_MoR_seed46__fb91cdff/checkpoint.pt

